# Local Home Assistant instances used to verify the home bridge against a real
# house. Every one of them holds refresh tokens and a long-lived access token in
# .storage/auth, so the pattern is deliberately broad: any .ha-* directory at the
# repo root is a throwaway HA instance and never belongs in a commit.
.ha-*/
# Same thing at fleet scale: scripts/home-fleet.mjs boots numbered Home Assistant
# instances under .home-fleet/<n>/, each with its own token store.
.home-fleet/
# The fleet registry that pairs those instances with their long-lived access
# tokens. Local state about local containers; the tokens make it uncommittable.
tasks/home/*.local.json

# Browser voice-loop runtime staged from node_modules by scripts/copy-voice-models.mjs
# (silero VAD + the onnxruntime-web wasm). Regenerated on every install and
# prebuild; the committed openWakeWord models under public/models/voice/wake-word
# are release artifacts and DO belong in git.
public/models/voice/runtime/
